## What needs operator wiring

Search `normalize_report.json` for `"todos"` to see the full list. Common
items:

- 🟧 **Forms** — every `<form>` has `data-original-action` set to the
  original endpoint. Wire it to Formspree, Netlify Forms, or your own
  backend when you're ready.
- 🟧 **Purchase buttons** (Buy / Subscribe / Upgrade) — left in place but
  flagged with `data-todo="needs-operator-wiring"`. The runtime warns
  rather than executing — wire these manually so you choose where the
  money flows.
- 🟧 **Search forms** (skip-trace, etc.) — disabled by default. The
  original form costs credits to submit.

## Regenerating

The normalizer is idempotent — re-running on the same capture replaces
this directory. The defaults:

  * **AI on for per-page HTML** — semantic rewrite of each page.
    The high-value step. Default ON.
  * **AI off for CSS consolidation** — the deterministic base + components
    fallback is already production-quality (modern reset, button styles,
    utilities, component skeletons referencing your design tokens).
  * **AI off for runtime.js** — the deterministic runtime ships 7 patterns
    (menu, modal, sticky-header, cookie banner, form-prevent, purchase-warn,
    smooth-scroll). Good enough for nearly every site.

To regenerate with defaults (AI on pages only, ~1 LLM call per page):

```bash
python -m scripts.normalize \
    --capture {{ capture_dir }} \
    --output {{ output_dir }}
```

To opt into AI for CSS and/or runtime as well:

```bash
python -m scripts.normalize \
    --capture {{ capture_dir }} \
    --output {{ output_dir }} \
    --ai-css --ai-runtime
```

To regenerate entirely deterministically (no LLM calls — fastest):

```bash
python -m scripts.normalize \
    --capture {{ capture_dir }} \
    --output {{ output_dir }} \
    --mock
# or equivalent:
python -m scripts.normalize ... --no-ai-pages
```

Backend resolution (in priority order):
  1. `--mock` flag or `DNA_NORMALIZE_MOCK_LLM=1` → deterministic only
  2. `DNA_NORMALIZE_LLM_BACKEND=mock|cli|sdk` → explicit override
  3. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` set → anthropic SDK (pay-per-token)
  4. `claude` on PATH → CLI (uses your existing Claude Code OAuth login —
     no extra API key needed)
  5. Otherwise → mock
